course: dictionary
lesson: 5090
title: Intelligent: thinking well
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Intelligent means able to learn, understand and think well and quickly. People, animals and machines can all be intelligent. When you meet this word, look at the words around it, because they are the context and they give clues. «Pigs are among the most intelligent farm animals: they solve puzzles, learn names.» Solving puzzles and learning names are clever things to do, so intelligent must mean clever.
explain: Intelligent can also describe a good idea or answer. «An intelligent question» is a question that shows good thinking. In the story, «which was intelligent of Mole, because that was exactly what it was» tells us Mole's guess was a clever one. Try your meaning in the sentence to check it still makes sense.
explain: Look at the word forms too: intelligent, more intelligent, most intelligent. We say «the most intelligent animals», not «the intelligentest animals». Scientists also use the phrase «intelligent life», which means life able to think, perhaps on other planets.
fact: Intelligent means able to learn, understand and think well and quickly.
fact: Intelligent can describe people, animals and machines.
fact: «Dolphins and crows are intelligent animals.»
fact: «Intelligent software» means a machine or system that can act in a smart way.
fact: «Intelligent life» means life able to think, perhaps on other planets, and no confirmed alien signal has ever been found.
exercise: «Pigs are among the most intelligent farm animals: they solve puzzles, learn names.» What does intelligent mean here? | Friendly to farmers | Hungry and noisy | Large and heavy | *Clever, able to learn and think well
exercise: SETI scientists listen for signals from «intelligent life». What does intelligent life mean? | Very tiny living things | *Life able to think, perhaps on other planets | Life that lives only in water | Plants growing in a garden
exercise: Mole says the footsteps were «intelligent of Mole». What does intelligent suggest about his guess? | *It was a clever guess | It was a noisy guess | It was a sleepy guess | It was a slow guess
exercise: Which form is correct? «Pigs are the ___ intelligent farm animals.» | *most | intelligentest | more | mostest
test: A guide dog refuses an order that would lead its owner into danger. This is called intelligent disobedience. What does it mean? | Sleeping at the kerb | *Refusing an order because it would be dangerous | Obeying every order without thinking | Running away from its owner
test: Which word completes this? «Dolphins are highly ___ animals.» | *intelligent | Intelligence | intelligents | intelligently
exam: Which word means able to learn, understand and think well and quickly? | Hungry | Gentle | *Intelligent | Curious
